DEPENDS -- what each program needs besides its own binary=========================================================Generated by scanning every binary for absolute OS-9 paths.  Use it whencopying individual programs onto a disk of your own: the binary alone isoften not enough.A path listed here may be a file the program READS (copy it too) or one itCREATES at runtime (make sure the directory exists and is writable).  Thescan cannot tell those apart, so both are listed.  '--' marks a path not onthis disk: either the program creates it, or its data was never collected.Most entries are /h0/sys/termcap -- 70 programs want termcap at that exactpath.  DOC/README-RUNNING explains how to arrange /h0.--------------------------------------------------------------  X11R6shl   (CMDS)      /dd/INCDIR/bitmaps                             --      /dd/LIBDIR/Xcms.txt                            --      /dd/LIBDIR/XErrorDB                            --      /dd/LIBDIR/XKeysymDB                           --      /dd/LIBDIR/XtErrorDB                           --      /dd/XLOCALEDIR                                 --      /dd/XTFILES                                    --  advent   (CMDS/GAMES)      /dd/GAMES/adv/glorkz                           --      /dd/GAMES/adv/tmp.foo.baz                      --  aterm   (CMDS)      /DD/SYS/ATERM/ATerm.Ctl                        --      /DD/SYS/ATERM/ATerm.Phone                      --      /DD/SYS/ATERM/ATerm.Print                      --  bash   (CMDS)      /dd/local/sys/profile                                /dd/SYS/errmsg                                       /dd/sys/password                                     /dd/sys/profile                                      /dd/tmp/                                             /h0/SYS/errmsg                                       /h0/sys/password                                     /dd/sys/termcap                                      /h0/sys/termcap                 